{"connection_id": "BC-a8492b97e66c063df470", "ref": "Augustine, Confessions 1.1.1", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "praise as the creature's response to its maker", "note": "The commentary places hamd before naming the specific gift; Augustine opens by praising God as creator and says human beings are made for God, so praise is the fitting response to dependence itself."}
{"connection_id": "BC-28c4333996e53e67f15e", "ref": "Didache 1.1", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "yaşam ve ölümün iki yolu", "note": "Didache yaşam yolu ile ölüm yolunu karşı karşıya koyar; 1:7'deki toplulukların ayrılan yollarına erken Hristiyan etik köprü kurar."}
{"connection_id": "BC-054f3543a22720676376", "ref": "Didache 10.2", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanksgiving for gifts of knowledge and life", "note": "The commentary says praise follows what God gives; after the meal the community thanks the holy Father for his name, knowledge, faith, and immortality given through Jesus."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0b157ef4b6fcdc348a77", "ref": "Didache 10.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "food given so people may thank the creator", "note": "The commentary says recipients answer God's provision with hamd; the post-meal prayer says God gave food and drink to humanity so that people might thank him, then names the community's spiritual food and drink."}
{"connection_id": "BC-74a9d3881f1cef9581c4", "ref": "Didache 10.5", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the prayer ends in glory to God", "note": "The commentary says the opening hamd returns at the end of the path; the Didache's thanksgiving closes by ascribing glory to God forever."}
{"connection_id": "BC-7225be8a66de358c77c8", "ref": "Didache 4:7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "verirken homurdanmamak", "note": "Didache verirken tereddüt etmemeyi ve homurdanmamayı söyler; armağanı alıcıya serzeniş yapmama yönünde erken Hristiyan etik paraleldir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2cc16b5b74e6915f38fb", "ref": "Didache 9.1", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanksgiving over cup and bread", "note": "The commentary makes hamd the recipient's response to a gift; the community's meal prayer gives thanks over the cup and broken bread as gifts from God through Jesus."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2bee712ca9a863a25ba2", "ref": "Didache 9.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "gathering the Church as one people", "note": "The commentary says favor belongs to a community and its path; the Eucharistic prayer asks that the scattered Church be gathered into God's kingdom, like bread once scattered and made one."}
{"connection_id": "BC-1ba557d4f1b6cab5858e", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.1.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanks for grace given in Christ", "note": "The commentary makes praise the response to a received gift; Paul thanks God for grace given to the Corinthian believers in Christ."}
{"connection_id": "BC-92d6f32fe3daa5a4cb4b", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.1.8", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God sustains believers to the end", "note": "The commentary links a completed favor to a walked path; Paul says Christ will strengthen the community to the end, blameless at his day."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e1decffa6228d2b966b", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.15.10", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "work attributed to grace rather than self", "note": "The commentary warns against presenting one's own effort as a merit; Paul says he worked hard, yet attributes what he is and his work to God's grace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-691f719e42c5b3738064", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.4.7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "what was received leaves no ground to boast", "note": "The commentary warns against advertising what one spent as one's own merit; Paul asks what anyone has that was not received and rejects boasting as though it were not received."}
{"connection_id": "BC-0e6b256766c7e53a95f5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Cor.4.7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "aldığını kendi malı gibi övünmemek", "note": "Her şeyi almış olanın, almamış gibi övünmemesi, nimeti kendi başarı ya da başkasına karşı üstünlük diye göstermeyi tersine çevirir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-3af528d7182408c4e805", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "received goods shared with a brother", "note": "The commentary's hand-to-hand image traces good from giver to recipient; John asks how God's love can remain in someone who sees a needy brother and closes the heart despite possessing the world's goods."}
{"connection_id": "BC-dbf8e486d239f9f7fbd8", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.3.18", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love enacted rather than merely spoken", "note": "The commentary contrasts genuine praise and giving with words that claim merit; John requires love in deed and truth, giving the response a practical form."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cb74fb627a527e27ffac", "ref": "SBLGNT:1John.4.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "love as a response to prior love", "note": "The commentary makes the recipient's response follow the giver's favor; John says believers love because God first loved them."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e81af4c0d3caf6f6ff8e", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "blessing God for new birth and hope", "note": "The commentary makes hamd the answer to a favor; Peter blesses God for new birth to a living hope through Jesus' resurrection."}
{"connection_id": "BC-c4b13eeffd35a74529f1", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "merhamet sebebiyle yeniden doğuş", "note": "Tanrı bereketlenir; büyük merhametine göre yeniden doğuş vermiştir: hamd ile ihsanın kaynak-sonuç dizilişidir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e863d50ba8ac8b81d009", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "an inheritance kept for recipients", "note": "The commentary says the favor belongs to a community and its path; Peter names an imperishable inheritance kept in heaven for believers."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d6887313b4029e7c88d5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.1.7", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faith tested toward praise and honor", "note": "The commentary makes the path end in a completed favor; Peter says tested faith will result in praise, glory, and honor at Jesus' revelation."}
{"connection_id": "BC-4837e351715cb9f81d04", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.10", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "once not a people, now recipients of mercy", "note": "The commentary identifies a community by the favor it received; Peter says those once outside the people have become God's people and have received mercy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-87c261229fb2b21b2c45", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "called from darkness to proclaim praises", "note": "The commentary asks for the path of people favored by God; Peter describes a people called from darkness into marvelous light to proclaim God's excellencies."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8cd6b380229ecaa7c115", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.2.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "faziletlerini ilan etmek", "note": "Seçilmiş topluluğun kendisini karanlıktan ışığa çağıranın erdemlerini ilan etmesi, lütfu başkalarına sayan ortak hamddir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-e9b1187cca31617c39a5", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.4.10", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "stewarding a gift for one another", "note": "The commentary pictures favor as good delivered to another; Peter tells each person to use the gift received to serve others as a steward of God's varied grace."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8d0990acf8227b5e7846", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Pet.4.10", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "alınan armağanı birbirine hizmette kullanmak", "note": "Herkes aldığı armağanı birbirine hizmet etmekte kullanır; iyiliğin bir elden ötekine ulaştırılması olarak in‘âmın cemaat içi biçimidir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b512bcb7cabe7ede2989", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.4.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "yiyeceği şükranla kabul etmek", "note": "Tanrı'nın yarattığı her iyi şeyin şükranla kabul edildiğinde reddedilmemesi, rızka verilen açık Hristiyan teşekkür cevabıdır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-32ce8a9b7a038dac883d", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.6.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "riches are gifts, not grounds for pride", "note": "The commentary rejects self-credit for what one has received; Paul tells the rich not to be arrogant but to hope in God, who richly provides all things to enjoy."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cfeb5b8d28c821707a64", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.6.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "zevk için bolca sağlayan Tanrı", "note": "Tanrı'nın zevk almak için her şeyi bolca sağladığı sözü, en‘ame'nin fazlasını verme ve artırma yönüne açık fakat anlatısız bir karşılıktır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-f0552db19b5453ed6028", "ref": "SBLGNT:1Tim.6.18", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "received wealth used generously for others", "note": "The commentary depicts good passing from hand to hand; Paul tells the wealthy to do good, be generous, and ready to share."}
{"connection_id": "BC-691be9dcc358952abdf2", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God as Father of mercies", "note": "The commentary names mercy as the source of good; Paul blesses the Father of mercies and God of all comfort."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b957a44daa4f67d7e81b", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "merhametlerin Babası", "note": "Bereket formülü Tanrı'yı merhametlerin Babası ve her tesellinin Tanrısı diye över; rahmetin iyilik kaynağı oluşunu Hristiyan doxolojisine taşır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-099ea98128fa51f083cf", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.1.4", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "comfort received and passed to others", "note": "The commentary pictures beneficence moving from giver to recipient; Paul says God comforts believers so they can comfort others in the trouble they themselves have received comfort through."}
{"connection_id": "BC-2d9eec102d3fc761a7af", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.15", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "grace multiplying thanksgiving to God's glory", "note": "The commentary says the recipient's praise follows God's favor; Paul says grace reaching more people multiplies thanksgiving to God's glory."}
{"connection_id": "BC-cdf26b0604a14c9d2d88", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.4.15", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lütuf yayılırken şükranın artması", "note": "Lütuf daha çok kişiye yayıldıkça şükranın Tanrı'nın yüceliğine çoğalması, verilen iyiliğin başkaları arasında hamde dönüşmesiyle örtüşür."}
{"connection_id": "BC-035c051401e167c993f3", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.8.6", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "χάρις hizmetini tamamlama", "note": "Titus'tan, başlattığı χάρις yani bağış toplama iyiliğini tamamlaması istenir; bu, iyiliğin sonuna kadar yapılması motifidir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-224032f87afb27f09b89", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.11", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "generosity producing thanksgiving", "note": "The commentary says the giver's good reaches a recipient who praises; Paul says generosity enriches the giver and produces thanksgiving to God through the recipients."}
{"connection_id": "BC-93a0bebdd0196341036b", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.11", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "zenginleştiren lütuf ve çoğalan şükran", "note": "Her cömertlik için her bakımdan zenginleştirilmek, elçiler aracılığıyla Tanrı'ya şükran doğurur; artırılmış nimet ile hamdin zinciridir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-765785a821626a9a91b8", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.12", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "need supplied and many thanksgivings", "note": "The commentary links conveyed good with praise of its source; Paul says the service supplies the saints' needs and overflows in many thanksgivings to God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-49208002c244364a42ca", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.13", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "recipients glorify God", "note": "The commentary depicts beneficiaries recounting the giver's good; Paul says recipients glorify God for the donors' confession and generous sharing."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6900a59bf974f9a00e4a", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.15", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "thanks for God's inexpressible gift", "note": "The commentary says praise answers a gift; Paul closes the account of giving by thanking God for his inexpressible gift."}
{"connection_id": "BC-24d0d78aed42d0413e37", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.15", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "tarif edilemez armağan için şükür", "note": "Tanrı'nın tarif edilemez armağanına şükür, bağış karşısındaki doğrudan cevap olarak durur."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d0caa3f4154385cc7424", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.8", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "abundant grace and sufficiency", "note": "The commentary's B010 branch says giving may exceed what is sufficient; Paul says God can make grace abound so believers have sufficiency for every good work."}
{"connection_id": "BC-a3b49195e3b0aed3df4a", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Cor.9.8", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "lütfun çoğalması ve her iyi iş", "note": "Tanrı lütfu bol bol artırır ki alıcılar her iyi iş için yeterli olsun; yorumdaki en‘ame “artırdı” ile tamamlanan ihsanı tek bağlamda tutar."}
{"connection_id": "BC-bd9a440df95620937ae0", "ref": "SBLGNT:2Pet.1.3", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "divine power grants what leads to life", "note": "The commentary joins bestowed favor with a path to walk; Peter says God's power has granted everything needed for life and godliness, calling believers by glory and excellence."}
{"connection_id": "BC-623baaa3742e68e3f47b", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.14.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "food, gladness, and witness to God's goodness", "note": "The commentary connects divine favor to the provision of good; Paul says God gave rain, fruitful seasons, food, and gladness, leaving witness among the nations."}
{"connection_id": "BC-d0700c059eaca7f86064", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.14.17", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "iyilik, yağmur ve yiyecek", "note": "Tanrı'nın iyilik yapıp yağmur, verimli mevsimler ve yiyecekle doyurması, 106:3–4'teki besleyen Rabbe kamusal elçi tanıklığıdır."}
{"connection_id": "BC-b0181230cb49f53c38c5", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.17.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "God gives life and breath to all", "note": "The commentary describes the giver as the source of good; Paul says God is not served as though needy, since he himself gives all people life, breath, and everything."}
{"connection_id": "BC-abb5e28189f81301cfd4", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.17.25", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "hayat, soluk ve her şeyi veren", "note": "Her insana hayatı, soluğu ve her şeyi veren Tanrı, 1:2'deki bütün âlemlerin Rabbine evrensel sağlayıcı olarak karşılık verir."}
{"connection_id": "BC-36c4ee48ac32ea01136d", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.20.35", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "vermenin almaktan daha bereketli oluşu", "note": "İsa'ya atfedilen vermenin almaktan daha bereketli olduğu sözü, yorumun elden ele geçen iyilik imgesine belirgin ama daha genel bir etik paralel sağlar."}
{"connection_id": "BC-73004c1e4c746afd68ed", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.3.8", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the healed man walks and praises God", "note": "The commentary joins a received favor to its path and response; the healed man enters the temple walking and leaping while praising God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-acc2eae07d571481a568", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.3.9", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "the public sees the recipient praising", "note": "The commentary says the beneficiary can voice praise before others; everyone sees the formerly lame man walking and praising God."}
{"connection_id": "BC-8e5cb123e9ae7733c40a", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.7.19", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Firavun'un halka zulmü", "note": "Firavun'un soya kötü davranıp bebekleri ölüme bırakması, sarayda büyütülmeyi lütuf sayan sözün baskı politikasıyla gerilimini Hristiyan anlatıda da kurar."}
{"connection_id": "BC-89c7d4a14791b7e349a8", "ref": "SBLGNT:Acts.7.21", "target": "sec5", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "karsi_anlati", "basis": "Pharaoh's daughter takes Moses as her son", "note": "The commentary places the claim of raising Moses in Pharaoh's mouth; Stephen's retelling attributes his rescue and adoption to Pharaoh's daughter, preserving the household upbringing but changing the agent."}
